-- `beforeSession` is awaited before the `try` block opens ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L91](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L91)), so a throw there escapes before the `catch`/`finally` exist and skips both `onError` and `afterSession`.
+- `beforeSession` is inside the `try` block, so a throw there reaches the `catch`/`finally` blocks and propagates to the caller as a rejection ([validated by: rejects when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L32)).
+- When `beforeSession` throws, `onError` is called with the same argument shape as any other orchestrator failure ([validated by: calls onError when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L48)).
+- When `beforeSession` throws, `afterSession` is called even though the turn was aborted before provider interaction and no tools were run — a deployer can assume `beforeSession` may not have fully completed ([validated by: calls afterSession when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L71)).
 - The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
 - `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L148](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L148)), and is passed the `lastUsage` local — the most recent round's usage, not a sum across tool rounds, so a deployer using the hook for billing or audit under-counts every turn that ran tools.
